{% macro imports() -%}
from confluent_kafka.schema_registry.rules.encryption.gcpkms.gcp_driver import GcpKmsDriver
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro register() -%}
GcpKmsDriver.register()
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro setup_credentials() -%}
# GCP service-account fields are passed via rule.executors._default_.param.* below;
# without these, the GCP driver silently falls back to Application Default Credentials
# (gcloud auth application-default login) and authenticates as a different identity.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro executor_params() -%}
'client.id': os.getenv('GCP_CLIENT_ID'),
'client.email': os.getenv('GCP_CLIENT_EMAIL'),
'private.key.id': os.getenv('GCP_PRIVATE_KEY_ID'),
'private.key': os.getenv('GCP_PRIVATE_KEY'),
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro env_vars() -%}
# Google Cloud KMS Configuration (for field-level encryption)
GCP_KMS_KEY_NAME={{ kek_name }}
GCP_KMS_TYPE=gcp-kms
GCP_KMS_KEY_ID={{ kms_params.kms_key_id or '<FILL_ME>' }}

# Google Cloud Service Account fields (extracted from the SA JSON file)
GCP_CLIENT_ID={{ kms_params.client_id or '<FILL_ME>' }}
GCP_CLIENT_EMAIL={{ kms_params.client_email or '<FILL_ME>' }}
GCP_PRIVATE_KEY_ID={{ kms_params.private_key_id or '<FILL_ME>' }}
# Single-line PEM with literal `\n` escapes; the surrounding double quotes are required so
# python-dotenv (and dotenv-java after the in-getter fix) can recognize it as a string value.
GCP_PRIVATE_KEY="{{ kms_params.private_key or '<FILL_ME>' }}"
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro pip_deps() -%}
confluent-kafka[avro,rules]=={{ confluent_kafka_version }}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro readme_section() -%}
This client encrypts the `birthday` field using **Google Cloud KMS**. You'll need:

* A **Google Cloud KMS keyring + key** (the KEK). The resource ID has the form `projects/<project>/locations/<loc>/keyRings/<ring>/cryptoKeys/<key>`.
* A **service account** with `Cloud KMS CryptoKey Encrypter/Decrypter` role on that key.
* The service account's JSON key file. Open it and copy the four fields `client_id`, `client_email`, `private_key_id`, and `private_key` into your `.env`.

> ⚠️ **Do not append `/cryptoKeyVersions/N`** to `GCP_KMS_KEY_ID`. Version-scoped resources are encrypt-only and CSFLE will fail on the very first produce when it tries to decrypt the DEK. Use the `cryptoKey` itself.

> **Note on `GCP_PRIVATE_KEY`:** the value is a multi-line PEM string with literal `\n` escapes. Wrap it in double quotes in `.env` so `python-dotenv` preserves the newlines.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro kms_type() -%}
gcp-kms
{%- endmacro %}
